# Help24 — Android release signing (TEMPLATE)
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `android/key.properties` and fill in. That file, and any .jks or
# .keystore anywhere under android/, are gitignored — by android/.gitignore
# AND by the repo root .gitignore. Never commit either, and never paste these
# values into a ticket, a chat message or a build log.
#
# If this file is absent, app/build.gradle falls back to these environment
# variables instead (the CI path):
#
#   HELP24_KEYSTORE_PATH       absolute path to the decoded .jks
#   HELP24_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD
#   HELP24_KEY_ALIAS
#   HELP24_KEY_PASSWORD
#
# If NEITHER is present, a release build fails with an explicit message. It
# does not fall back to the debug key — a debug-signed release breaks Google
# Sign-In and phone verification on every real device, and does so silently.
#
# Create the keystore once (keep the backup somewhere you will still have in
# five years — losing it means you can never update the app under this
# identity again):
#
#   keytool -genkeypair -v \
#     -keystore %USERPROFILE%/help24-release.jks \
#     -storetype JKS -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 \
#     -alias help24
#
# Then read its fingerprints and register BOTH with the identity provider:
#
#   keytool -list -v -keystore %USERPROFILE%/help24-release.jks -alias help24
#
# Full procedure, including the Play App Signing certificate: _docs/ANDROID_BUILD.md
# =============================================================================

# Absolute path preferred. A relative path is resolved against android/.
storeFile=C:/Users/<you>/help24-release.jks

storePassword=<the keystore password>
keyAlias=help24
keyPassword=<the key password — often the same as storePassword>
